[statement]
apk reads a name where the index first mentions it, as a record's own
name or an entry of its dependencies, provides or `install_if`, whether
or not that record is installed, and a list's entries in the order
stated. `other` mentions `xp` before `au`, so `au` is read last and comes
first of the two, which share a bucket.

[repository]
P:other
V:1
D:xp au

P:base
V:1

P:au
V:1
i:base

P:xp
V:1
i:base

[request]
base

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install base 1
install au 1
install xp 1
